<figure class="r42-lookup" data-r42-lookup aria-labelledby="r42-lookup-title">
 <figcaption id="r42-lookup-title"><span>Figure 1</span> The same caller, two different sources of a price</figcaption>
 <p class="note">Illustrative steps checked by the native counterexample · caller remains runtime_10</p>
 <div class="identity"><span>Session identity <strong>runtime_10</strong></span><span>Effective identity <strong data-live data-effective></strong></span></div>
 <div class="relations"><div data-temp><strong>Caller’s temporary products</strong><p>P7 · forged value 999</p><span data-live data-temp-state></span></div><div data-real><strong>shop.products</strong><p>Shop 10 · Blue mug · 20.00</p><span data-live data-real-state></span></div></div>
 <p class="rule" data-live data-rule></p><p class="result" data-live data-result></p>
 <p class="explanation" data-live data-explanation aria-live="polite"></p>
 <div class="controls"><fieldset><legend>Privileged lookup</legend><label><input type="radio" name="r42-lookup" value="unsafe" checked /> Unqualified owner lookup</label><label><input type="radio" name="r42-lookup" value="safe" /> Qualified, limited lookup</label></fieldset><div class="buttons"><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step aria-label="Step"></span></div><div data-hold class="hold" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div></div>
 <details><summary>The complete lookup, as text</summary><p>The caller owns a temporary products table containing forged price 999 and has granted the unsafe function owner permission to read it. The unsafe SECURITY DEFINER lookup runs as shop_owner and resolves unqualified products to that temporary table. The corrected lookup runs as catalogue_code, names shop.products explicitly and uses a policy based on the original runtime_10 session identity. It returns the real shop 10 price, 20.00. Neither routine changes the stored catalogue in this comparison.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
 import {stepper} from '../../figures/stepper.mjs';
 document.querySelectorAll('[data-r42-lookup]').forEach(root=>{
  const player=stepper(root,{steps:()=>5,draw:n=>{
   const safe=root.querySelector('input:checked').value==='safe';
   root.querySelector('[data-effective]').textContent=n===0?'runtime_10':safe?'catalogue_code':'shop_owner';
   root.querySelector('[data-temp-state]').textContent=n<2?'Not looked up':safe?'Not referenced':'Selected by unqualified name';
   root.querySelector('[data-real-state]').textContent=n<2?'Not looked up':safe?'Selected by qualified name':'Not reached';
   root.querySelector('[data-temp]').dataset.selected=String(n>=2&&!safe);root.querySelector('[data-real]').dataset.selected=String(n>=2&&safe);
   root.querySelector('[data-rule]').textContent=n<3?'No row returned yet':safe?'Row policy: session_user maps to shop 10':'Forged row is read under the function’s authority';
   root.querySelector('[data-result]').textContent=n<4?'Result pending':safe?'Returned price: 20.00':'Returned price: 999';
   root.querySelector('[data-explanation]').textContent=(safe?[
    'runtime_10 is the authenticated session identity. It cannot become the owner or catalogue_code.',
    'Calling the SECURITY DEFINER function changes current_user to catalogue_code. session_user remains runtime_10.',
    'The function names shop.products explicitly. The caller’s temporary products table is not a candidate for that name.',
    'catalogue_code has SELECT and a policy that derives shop 10 from session_user. It has no table ownership or bypass attribute.',
    'The real Blue mug price is 20.00. The same temporary table and caller setting cannot redirect this lookup.'
   ]:[
    'runtime_10 owns a temporary products table with price 999. It grants shop_owner permission to read that counterfeit table.',
    'The SECURITY DEFINER function runs as shop_owner. This does not change who originally opened the session.',
    'The function sets search_path to shop but uses unqualified products. Because pg_temp is not explicitly placed, its relation name is searched first.',
    'The caller’s forged relation is readable under the function’s authority. The intended shop table and its tenant policy never decide this result.',
    'The function returns 999. The real Blue mug still costs 20.00: the privileged lookup read the wrong relation.'
   ])[n];
  }});
  root.querySelectorAll('input').forEach(input=>input.addEventListener('change',()=>player.render()));
 });
</script>
<style>
